@startuml sequence-invite

!define THEME_COLOR #2E86AB

title INVITE Module Flow\nSend Invitation → Email → Verify → Accept

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceParticipantPadding 20
skinparam sequenceBoxBorderColor #CCCCCC

skinparam sequence {
    ActorBorderColor #2E86AB
    ActorBackgroundColor #D6EAF8
    ParticipantBorderColor #A23B72
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F5E6CC
    DatabaseBorderColor #1B998B
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #D4EDDA
    QueueBorderColor #F18F01
    QueueBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
    ArrowColor #333333
    LifeLineBorderColor #999999
    ArrowFontSize 11
    ParticipantFontSize 13
    ParticipantFontSize 12
}

' ============================================================
' Participants
' ============================================================
actor "HR / Employer" as HR #2E86AB
participant "Frontend\n(Browser)" as FE #C84B31
participant "RECR / INVITE\nService (NestJS)" as INVITE #A23B72
database "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB #1B998B
queue "RabbitMQ" as MQ #F18F01
participant "EMAIL\nService" as EMAIL #E8AA14
actor "Candidate" as CAND #5B8C5A
participant "AUTH\nService" as AUTH #6A4C93

' ============================================================
' Phase 1: Send Invitation
' ============================================================
== Phase 1: Send Invitation ==

HR -> FE : Fill invite form\n(email, role)
FE -> INVITE : POST /invitations/send\n{email, role, employerId}

note right of INVITE
  **Validation:**
  - Check email format
  - Check role is valid enum
  - Check employer exists
  - Check no duplicate pending invite
end note

INVITE -> DB : INSERT INTO invitations\n(token_hash, email, role,\nemployer_id, status = 'PENDING',\nexpires_at)
note right of DB
  Token is generated as a
  random UUID / crypto token.
  Only the SHA-256 **hash**
  is stored in the database.
end note

INVITE -> MQ : Emit "invitation.created"\n{invitationId, email,\ntoken, employerId}

MQ -> EMAIL : Consume event

EMAIL -> CAND : Send email with\ninvite link:\n/invite?token={raw_token}

note over CAND
  Email contains a deep link
  with the **raw token** in the
  query string. The token is
  never stored in plaintext.
end note

' ============================================================
' Phase 2: Verify Token
' ============================================================
== Phase 2: Verify Token ==

CAND -> FE : Click link in email\n/invite?token={raw_token}

FE -> INVITE : GET /invitations/verify?token={raw_token}

note right of INVITE
  **Security:**
  The service hashes the raw
  token with SHA-256 and looks
  up the invitation by
  `token_hash` — never by
  the raw token directly.
end note

INVITE -> INVITE : hash(token) → token_hash\nlookup by token_hash

INVITE -> DB : SELECT * FROM invitations\nWHERE token_hash = ?\nAND status = 'PENDING'

alt Invitation is valid and not expired
    INVITE --> FE : 200 OK\n{email, role, employerId,\ninvitationId}
else Invitation expired
    INVITE --> FE : 410 Gone\n"Invitation has expired"
else Invitation not found
    INVITE --> FE : 404 Not Found\n"Invitation not found"
else Invitation already accepted
    INVITE --> FE : 400 Bad Request\n"Invitation already accepted"
end

' ============================================================
' Phase 3: Accept Invitation
' ============================================================
== Phase 3: Accept Invitation ==

CAND -> FE : Fill registration form\n(name, password, ...)

FE -> INVITE : POST /invitations/accept\n{invitationId, name, password}

note right of INVITE
  **Pre-checks:**
  1. Verify invitation status
     is still PENDING
  2. Re-verify token hasn't
     expired
  3. Validate password strength
end note

INVITE -> DB : UPDATE invitations\nSET status = 'ACCEPTED',\naccepted_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = ?\nAND status = 'PENDING'

note right of DB
  Uses a conditional UPDATE
  (WHERE status = 'PENDING')
  to prevent race conditions.
  Returns 0 rows if already
  accepted.
end note

INVITE -> MQ : Emit "invitation.accepted"\n{invitationId, email, name,\nemployerId, role}

MQ -> AUTH : Consume event

AUTH -> DB : INSERT/UPDATE users\nSET email = ?, name = ?,\nrole = ?, employer_id = ?,\nstatus = 'ACTIVE'

note right of AUTH
  AUTH service creates or
  activates the user account.
  If user already exists,
  it may merge or reject
  depending on business rules.
end note

AUTH --> MQ : Ack (success)

INVITE --> FE : 200 OK\n{success: true,\nmessage: "Account created"}

' ============================================================
' Legend
' ============================================================
legend bottom left
  |= Symbol |= Description |
  | **PENDING** | Invitation created, awaiting candidate action |
  | **ACCEPTED** | Candidate accepted; user account activated |
  | **EXPIRED** | Token TTL exceeded (checked on verify/accept) |
  | **REVOKED** | HR cancelled the invitation before acceptance |
  ----
  **Security Notes:**
  - Raw token is never stored; only SHA-256 hash is persisted
  - Verify endpoint checks status = PENDING and expiry
  - Accept uses conditional UPDATE to prevent race conditions
  - Events are idempotent; AUTH service deduplicates by invitationId
  ----
  **Color Legend:**
  <back:#2E86AB>  </back> HR/Employer
  <back:#C84B31>  </back> Frontend
  <back:#A23B72>  </back> INVITE Service
  <back:#1B998B>  </back> Database
  <back:#F18F01>  </back> RabbitMQ
  <back:#E8AA14>  </back> EMAIL Service
  <back:#5B8C5A>  </back> Candidate
  <back:#6A4C93>  </back> AUTH Service
endlegend

@enduml
